aken/1095945-2e-mortal-cults-as-antagonists?p=1096061#post1096061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean cultists and demon summoners? Are you asking how to make them antagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div>I ask how to make the <b>cult</b> as proper antagonist for werewolves. What tactics would cultists apply to their workings? How much they would anticipate about weaknesses of werewolves? How influencial they can be? Some storytelling adivce on those subject will be much appreciate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T00:05:52-07:00","id":1096189,"title":"","content":"Hugely depends on what sort of group and infrastructure the cult is embedded into. A fraternity, a bunch of accountants, a high-class society of businessmen, a political party, a local gang, a labor union, and a ring of university professors all have different areas of expertise and tools of the trade they can harass werewolves with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T04:01:30-07:00","id":1096217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1095945-2e-mortal-cults-as-antagonists?p=1096056#post1096056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be an issue for storm lords not iron masters.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? You think every antagonist a pack (particularly a single tribe pack) would face neatly fit into their favored prey? Storm Lords would get what? A +2 to affect them with facets and/or rites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T04:17:01-07:00","id":1096226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1095945-2e-mortal-cults-as-antagonists?p=1096217#post1096217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So? You think every antagonist a pack (particularly a single tribe pack) would face neatly fit into their favored prey?</div> </div> </div> </div>No... but the OP specifically was talking about making a foe for Iron Masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T05:33:17-07:00","id":1096251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1095945-2e-mortal-cults-as-antagonists?p=1096226#post1096226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No... but the OP specifically was talking about making a foe for Iron Masters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cults obey a mythology that serves their figurehead, a cult headed by a Claimed is still a cult. If the themes of the game observe spiritual corruption, few things could be as corrupting. The rest of the organization is still comprises of mortals, Iron Master's given prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T09:24:14-07:00","id":1108786,"title":"","content":"The neat thing about Mystery Cult Initiation is that mortals, Claimed, Hosts, and werewolves can have it, and there can be spirits which are fed by the cult, making the whole thing great for any pack.<br /> <br /> I have made a mystery cult with Slenderman as a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/799082-cofd-diy-mystery-cults?p=1108502#post1108502\">member/founder</a>, and that cult would be particularly hard for werewolves to deal with. I am envisioning a story line where a pack member wolfblooded, mortal or even a PC werewolf that's likely to become obsessed with mysteries to get drawn into the Mystery Cult through investigating the Slenderman urban legend, and then the rest of the pack having to deal with member who has the Slender Sickness Condition, possibly confronting Slenderman to no avail.<br /> Ultimately the only ways to deal with Slender Sickness is the ability to cause Amnesia, isolate the victim so they can't spread it, or kill them for the same reason.","